  {
   "text": "\u2248 1 Jev call \u00b7 the LLM only fills a free-text argument \u00b7 lowest cost and latency",
   "x": 150,
   "y": 166,
   "font_size": 11,
   "color": "#6B7280",
   "anchor": "start"
  },
  {
   "text": "1 short LLM call to enumerate + 1 Jev call to choose \u00b7 the LLM does not act",
   "x": 150,
   "y": 291,
   "font_size": 11,
   "color": "#6B7280",
   "anchor": "start"
  },
  {
   "text": "1 full LLM call per step \u00b7 used when the action space is open, confidence is low, or progress has stalled",
   "x": 150,
   "y": 416,
   "font_size": 11,
   "color": "#6B7280",
   "anchor": "start"
  },
  {
   "text": "The same step on the three paths. The router picks one per step; the guard runs on every path and forces escalation for irreversible actions regardless of confidence.",
   "x": 640,
   "y": 40,
   "font_size": 13,
   "color": "#374151",
   "anchor": "middle"
  },
  {
   "text": "What moves between paths over time: macro-action mining turns frequent LLM sequences into new Jev options, so open territory becomes closed territory.",
   "x": 640,
   "y": 460,
   "font_size": 12,
   "color": "#15803D",
   "anchor": "middle"
  },
